%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Squirrel
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 6
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Crystal Joust
    AbilityDescription: BASE (no upgrade needed) - joust a lifeform's crystal while
      moving faster than it to wither opposing-domain creatures, freeing the heart
      and auto-collecting it. Charge SCALING IS AN OPEN HOLE - the joust has no
      elemental parameter yet; it is deferred to the branch that reworks the joust,
      and this row is deliberately left without one rather than given a placeholder.
      At level 5 the joust also SHEPHERDS allies - an own-domain lifeform is
      NOURISHED instead (ILifeFormEntity.Nourish - its starvation clock resets and
      its birth counter advances).
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Shepherd
    UpgradeDescription: Jousting an OWN-domain lifeform's crystal nourishes it
      instead of doing nothing.
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Boost Ring
    AbilityDescription: Deploy a ring of conserved prism mass ahead of the vessel -
      the Squirrel's mass-creation ability, which is why it sits on Mass. Mass
      shortens the deploy cooldown (SquirrelTubeActionSO.cooldownMultiplierAtFullMass,
      x1 at rest -> x0.5 at level 10, floored), so a heavier pilot lays rings more
      often. At level 5 each deploy lays a second ring.
    Input: 11
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Twin Rings
    UpgradeDescription: The boost ring deploys with a second ring.
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Steal
    AbilityDescription: Skim a prism to STEAL it into your own domain. Space grows
      the skimmer sphere (authored on the skimmer's Scale ElementalFloat, 15 -> 30
      at level 10, evaluated live), and the sphere IS the steal reach - a bigger
      skimmer converts more mass per pass. BASE - an opposing SHIELDED prism only
      loses its shield and keeps its domain. At level 5 the steal goes through the
      shield - the prism changes hands AND keeps its armour. Super-shielded mass
      stays invulnerable at every level.
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Iron Grip
    UpgradeDescription: Shielded prisms are stolen outright and keep their shield,
      instead of merely being stripped of it.
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Skimming
    AbilityDescription: Time raises the boost energy gained per prism-skimmer
      collision (SkimmerBoostPrismEffectSO.energyMultiplier, x1 -> x2 at level 10
      floored at x0.25, read live per hit). Skim energy is the Squirrel's speed, so
      the element that makes the pilot faster owns it. At level 5 danger prisms
      grant the 10x energy bonus (below it they pay base energy - the bonus is
      earned, no longer always on).
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Live Wire
    UpgradeDescription: Danger prisms grant 10x boost energy when skimmed.
